Saturday night, I was sitting around waiting for some soup to finish
cooking when I decided to start up a neutral human barbarian, just to
have a bit of hack and slash fun.  I started near the left side of the
level and headed right.  In the next room, I found the downstairs, and
contemplated taking them.  I had a strange thought that, if I did, I'd
miss something good (not sure why I had this thought).  I decided to
map the entire level, at least to get to level 2 killing the grid
bugs, lichen, etc.

In the last room, to the north of my starting position, there's a
chest.  Having no good way to open it, I started kicking it.  I broke
no less than 3 potions before I got the chest opened.  Once the lock
broke, I found a food ration and a wand inside the chest.

Yes, you see where this is going.  E- hi, Ef You may wish for an
object.  Now, how in the hell did I know that was going to happen? 
Anyway, wished for 2 blessed scrolls of charging, had to recharge,
then got b+0GDSM, bf+3SB, bfg+3HoTele, and bf+0GoDex.  Did the gnomish
mines first (might as well... the gnomes can't take down this tank,
even if he is just wielding a +02HS).  Didn't bother clearing the
mines, just found the stairs, went down.  Got to the gnomish kings
wine cellar minend level, confiscated a pick-ax from (the corpse of) a
dwarf, dug out the gems, picked up the booze and went up to the main
dungeon, next stop Sokoban.

Descending to level 5, there's a wand across the room from the stairs.
 Another wand of wishing, turns out to be (0:2).  OK... this is
getting ridiculous, especially for a game I intended to last no more
than 30 minutes.  I went ahead and wished for a bf+3OilCl and
bf+3T-shirt.  Used my other b?oC to recharge it, wished up a blessed
